From baf71fdc6e7d583f06f53935e03d9bdd15f7cced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muse <muse@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:34:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] vendor: nix 0.31.3 with macOS-only utun gates for iOS

nix gates KextControl/UtunIfname on apple_targets, but libc defines
SYSPROTO_CONTROL / UTUN_OPT_IFNAME only on macOS, so nix fails to
compile for aarch64-apple-ios (E0425, pulled in by gotatun's unix nix
dependency with net/socket features). Vendor nix 0.31.3 and gate those
items (plus their GetCString helper) to target_os = "macos".

Rebased onto 5f1d090: upstream added vendor/h3, so the workspace
exclude list and vendor/PATCHES.md gained h3 rows; the patch hunks
were re-based onto the new line numbers. The vendored nix copy itself
is unchanged.
