+## nix-0.31.3-ios 0.31.3
+
+The package archive checksum is `cf20d2fde8ff38632c426f1165ed7436270b44f199fc55284c38276f9db47c3d`.
+
+- `src/sys/socket/mod.rs`: `KextControl` is macOS-only. nix gates it on `apple_targets` (any of
+  iOS/macOS/watchOS/tvOS/visionOS), but libc defines `SYSPROTO_CONTROL` only on macOS, so the crate does
+  not compile for `aarch64-apple-ios` (E0425). The gate is now `target_os = "macos"`.
+- `src/sys/socket/sockopt.rs`: `UtunIfname` and its `GetCString` helper are macOS-only, for the same
+  reason (`SYSPROTO_CONTROL` / `UTUN_OPT_IFNAME` are macOS-only in libc). Both gates are now
+  `target_os = "macos"`; without gating `GetCString` too, nix's `#![deny(unused)]` fails the iOS build
+  with "struct `GetCString` is never constructed".
+
 ## quinn 0.11.12
 
 - `src/endpoint.rs`, `src/endpoint/recv_buffer.rs`: receive scratch is leased from a thread-local cache only
